cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PySAD in your research, please cite the paper below."
title: "PySAD: A Streaming Anomaly Detection Framework in Python"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Selim Firat
    family-names: Yilmaz
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0486-7731"
repository-code: "https://github.com/selimfirat/pysad"
url: "https://pysad.readthedocs.io/"
license: BSD-3-Clause
abstract: >-
  PySAD is an open-source Python framework for anomaly detection on streaming
  multivariate data, providing online anomaly detection models, stream
  simulators, evaluators, preprocessors, postprocessors, probability
  calibrators and statistic trackers.
keywords:
  - anomaly detection
  - outlier detection
  - streaming data
  - online learning
  - machine learning
  - python
